Z||000000||Mark O'Hara||10-29-2000||10:47 PM||||What radiators will fit a Fiero? How can the cooling be improved simply I hope? What problems with engine cooling have been experienced with larger 6's and 8's? <BR>Thanks,<BR>Mark||||reg||5
Z||000001||PJ||10-30-2000||09:29 AM||||Ron Davis in AZ sell an all aluminum 2" radiator that is almost a perfect fit. Cost less than $200. I can look up the specs and phone # if you need them.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Zorba||10-30-2000||10:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by PJ:<BR><B>almost a perfect fit. Cost less than $200. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What is ? almost?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GTZ34||10-30-2000||01:21 PM||||Doesn't Archie have some upgrade dropins?  I was going to look there when I get ready to do mine.<P>------------------<BR>87GTZ34||||reg||1
Z||000004||Zorba||10-30-2000||01:32 PM|||| Archie has a real nice 4-core radiator for $325-$350 that does the job.||||reg||6
Z||000005||PJ||10-30-2000||03:22 PM||||Almost is 24" x 16" x 3" (not 2"). It is a NASCAR style all aluminum radiator with welded side tanks and the outlets are in the same positions as stock. The upper left one is 1.75" though so you need a reducer hose. The only problem with fitting is the 3" thickness. The top bracket needs to be modified a little. Price was $210 back in july '97.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mark O'Hara||10-30-2000||10:30 PM||||Hey! That sounds good to me. How do I get in touch with this company.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Mark||||reg||5
Z||000007||PJ||10-31-2000||05:32 PM||||Ron Davis Racing Products<BR>7334 N 108th Ave<BR>Glendale  AZ  85307<P>602-877-5000<P>Be advised this radiator has no cooler for an auto transaxle and if you have A/C you might have to move the condenser. Part # is RAD24163.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Archie||11-01-2000||08:38 AM||||PJ, do you actually have one of the Davis rads. in your car?<P>I've installed a few of these radiators and they didn't match your description. And required more modifications than you describe. <P>In an effort to keep conversion costs as low as I can while retaining quality. I'm always trying new parts. The Davis rads. I've used had the same measurements as you describe, but the cost was $400+ and the inlet/outlets were 1.5" in Dia. and were both located on the wrong side of the rad. Also the modifications to mount the radiator were extensive and, as a racing radiator they had no provision for an overflow tank connection.<P>Thanks<P>Archie||||reg||5
Z||000009||PJ||11-01-2000||06:31 PM||||Archie,<P>I was amazed at how easy the Davis radiator was to install. 1.75" inlet top left, 1.5" outlet lower right, filler neck in the upper right corner with a barbed overflow nipple. I literally threw it into the car in less than an hour on a Sat. morning so I could go racing here at Daytona after lunch.<P>Did you get a standard, off the shelf model or did you order something custom like a double pass? If they have changed or discontinued the design I got I'll be kicking myself for not buying a few of them.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||rockcrawl||11-01-2000||09:24 PM||||Griffin Radiator <A HREF="http://www.griffinrad.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.griffinrad.com/</A>  makes a radiator that fits fairly well. Their standard Nascar Chevy style is 3" taller than the stock one, and comes in various widths. I have used these in a few of my cars. The core is made of two rows of 1" tubes, the upper inlet is 1.5" and the lower outlet is 1.75". It has the filler with an overflow nipple in the stock location. They go for $182 from Summit or Jegs. They will make a custom one approx 16"x 24.5" with the correct size in/out tubes, but I don't recall the price they quoted me.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"||||reg||1
